#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:5
#: d8a94da5b33442b29e64054cd9c739b2
msgid "HeliQuads (Variable Pitch Multicopters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:10
#: c558378898a0475ab9bddfcd417ab5b7
msgid "ArduPilot supports HeliQuads, also called Collective Pitch Quadcopters or Variable Pitch Multicopters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:14
#: 1c1a73f68dd04fa198483ae5b1bebc79
msgid "Heli quad requires a :ref:`traditional helicopter <traditional-helicopters>` as the base firmware. It is available for download from the `firmware server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/>`__. When Copter is compiled, it now generates both traditional helicopter and multirotor firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:16
#: 3b35c499389049f0acac5a499997d119
msgid "These vehicles use independently controlled collective pitch on each of 4 rotors, with a single electric motor that powers all 4 rotors at the same speed via belts and a torque tube. It is highly aerobatic, capable of inverted flight but can suffer from :ref:`high vibration levels <common-measuring-vibration>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:20
#: fb034cb75ae1489989bb40e05e05abc7
msgid "Where to Buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:22
#: abef9d50014f4127964ec5b48bfc538d
msgid "WLtoys Assassin V383 is available from retailers including `WLtoys.eu <https://wltoys.eu/wltoys-v383>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:25
#: 7a8a14b248044085a0efbbeb607ecde8
msgid "Connecting and Configuring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:31
#: 3e8940d038454e13ba14241119582e70
msgid "each servo should be connected using the same outputs that would be used for motors on a regular multicopter (:ref:`see order here <connect-escs-and-motors>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:32
#: cdf35e8810d7459d99683027cc9c534a
msgid "the motor's ESC should be connected to the autopilot's channel 8 output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:33
#: 4e9eeafa441c464d94f0839617ba69c9
msgid ":ref:`traditional helicopter firmware <traditional-helicopters>` should be loaded onto the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:35
#: 515857556353448e863d8c6f771dee2d
msgid "If using the `WLToys Assassin V383 a parameter file is available here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/Frame_params/WLToys_V383_HeliQuad.param>`__ and can be used to set all parameters immediately. For other builds these are the standard params that should be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:38
#: 69c801f4b0b548ba9a87b46faf199618
msgid ":ref:`FRAME_CLASS <FRAME_CLASS>` to 13 (HeliQuad)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:39
#: f3828a9038124b3eaa03c7bebdc27935
msgid ":ref:`FRAME_TYPE <FRAME_CLASS>` to 1 (\"X\" if front right motors spins counter clockwise) or 3 (\"H\" if front right motor spins clockwise)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/heliquads.rst:41
#: 3e01d283803c44658a1dcdb8d85c9281
msgid "Similar to a :ref:`traditional helicopter <traditional-helicopters>` an :ref:`auxiliary switch <common-auxiliary-functions>` should be set to \"Motor Interlock\" to turn on/off the motor.  Normally this is channel 8 so you could set :ref:`RC8_OPTION<RC8_OPTION>` to 32."
msgstr ""

